Description: [security] Fix crash when the Upgrade header cannot be read (CVE-2024-37890)
 It is possible that the Upgrade header is correctly received and handled
 (the 'upgrade' event is emitted) without its value being returned to the
 user. This can happen if the number of received headers exceed the
 server.maxHeadersCount or request.maxHeadersCount threshold. In this case
 incomingMessage.headers.upgrade may not be set. Handle the case correctly
 and abort the handshake instead of crashing.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/websockets/ws/commit/eeb76d313e2a00dd5247ca3597bba7877d064a63
